entences:[{t:"Inna September 2025, di Oxford English Dictionary add some new word from di Caribbean.",en:"In September 2025, the Oxford English Dictionary added some new words from the Caribbean."},{t:"Two a di word dem a \"broughtupsy\" and \"bulla\".",en:"Two of the words are \"broughtupsy\" and \"bulla\"."},{t:"If smaddy have broughtupsy, it mean seh dem have good manners, because dem parents raise dem good.",en:"If someone has broughtupsy, it means they have good manners, because their parents raised them well."},{t:"Bulla a one sweet, dark cake weh people mek wid molasses and spice.",en:"Bulla is a sweet, dark cake that people make with molasses and spices."},{t:"Nuff people nyam bulla and pear, weh a di Jamaican word fi avocado.",en:"Lots of people eat bulla with pear, which is the Jamaican word for avocado."},{t:"Linguist dem seh dis a good news, because it show seh di world a listen to Caribbean voice dem.",en:"Linguists say this is good news, because it shows that the world is listening to Caribbean voices."},{t:"Di linguist Bertram Gayle seh Caribbean language dem a real language wid structure, not \"broken\" English.",en:"The linguist Bertram Gayle said Caribbean languages are real languages with structure, not \"broken\" English."},{t:"But im also seh wi need fi sort out di spelling, and im point to di Cassidy-JLU system.",en:"But he also said we need to sort out the spelling, and he pointed to the Cassidy-JLU system."},{t:"So next time yuh granny tell yuh seh yuh nuh have nuh broughtupsy, yuh can check it inna di dictionary!",en:"So next time your granny tells you that you've got no broughtupsy, you can look it up in the dictionary!"}],questions:[{q:"When did the OED add these words?",options:["June 1948","August 1962","September 2025"],answer:2},{q:"What does broughtupsy mean?",options:["Good manners from a good upbringing","A sweet cake","A type of music"],answer:0},{q:"What is bulla?",options:["A greeting","A sweet, dark cake","A dance"],answer:1}],g